# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in.
.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to the pipenv official documentation: https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/
#   Some files that are generated by pipenv should be ignored in the repository:
#   https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/basics.html#ignoring-the-pipfile-in-your-repository
Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock is expected to be committed in the repository
#   as a lock file to ensure reproducible builds, but it is not necessary to ignore it.
#   However, if you want to ignore it, uncomment the line below.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to poetry.lock, pdm.lock is expected to be committed in the repository
#   as a lock file to ensure reproducible builds, but it is not necessary to ignore it.
#   However, if you want to ignore it, uncomment the line below.
# pdm.lock

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/David-OConnor/pyflow and github.com/davidfelix/gutierrez.py
__pypackages__/

